Article 2 (Matters Subject to Reporting)
(1) The following matters shall be subject to reports on important audit results:
1. Important audit results related to national security;
2. Important audit results related to public safety or having significant repercussions on people's lives, for which improvements are urgently needed;
3. Important audit results involving concerns over large-scale budget waste or inefficiency in the operation of public finances or the implementation of major national projects;
4. Important audit results requiring timely measures because serious misconduct, such as passive administration or undermining discipline in public office, has been confirmed.
(2) Matters concerning important requests for disposition by the Board of Audit and Inspection that have not been implemented despite two or more reminders shall also be subject to reporting as provided in paragraph (1). In such cases, the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall apply mutatis mutandis to important requests for disposition.
